<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUT_NightsideIce                             UtinniPatches · authored 2026-09-07
    NIGHTSIDE_ICE_DEF_1. Full sheet: design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/nightside_ice.md.

    Own def, not a patch (owner's ruling, §0 of the sheet). Vanilla IceSheet carries an
    arctic zoo, coastal walrus/penguin, salmon/cod, snow at real commonality with
    DLC-gated blizzards, and pond terrainPatchMakers — patching all of that out across
    MayRequire branches is silent-failure territory, so this restates IceSheet's SHAPE
    directly and overrides every list to empty, per §6's hard bans.

    🔴 NOT ParentName="IceSheet". Verified against the real engine (ilprobe,
    Verse.XmlInheritance.TryRegister/GetBestParentFor): a ParentName only resolves
    against another def's Name="..." XML attribute, registered into a nodesByName
    dictionary — never against defName as a fallback. Vanilla IceSheet's own tag
    (Data/Core/Defs/BiomeDefs/Biomes_Cold.xml) has no Name= attribute at all, so
    ParentName="IceSheet" would silently fail to resolve (GetBestParentFor finds
    nothing in nodesByName for "IceSheet"). This is a real, engine-verified trap, not a
    style choice — restating the shape below is the only way to actually inherit it.

    Fields kept from vanilla IceSheet, verbatim: workerClass, allowFarmingCamps,
    allowRoads, allowRivers, isExtremeBiome, plantDensity, hasVirtualPlants, forageability,
    movementDifficulty, lakeBeachTerrain/mudTerrain, terrainsByFertility, texture
    (placeholder — the sheet's "dirty ice, not blue" art is separate, unowed work).
    Vanilla's own closing line survives as this def's epigraph (sheet §0: "Vanilla's one
    line survives as this sheet's epigraph"), quoted verbatim in the description below.

    Overridden to empty/zero, per §6's hard bans (no exceptions, no MayRequire branches
    to carry across — there is simply nothing here):
      wildAnimals, coastalWildAnimals, allowedPackAnimals — the arctic zoo is evicted
        (⛔ "no icy dayside analogs", ⛔ "no ordinary animal silhouettes at all").
      fishTypes, maxFishPopulation — ⛔ "no liquid water anywhere, in any form, ever".
      terrainPatchMakers — DROPPED entirely (not just emptied): vanilla's block generates
        WaterShallow ponds via perlin threshold, which is exactly the liquid-water ban.
      animalDensity 0 — nothing to scale (was 0.2).
      soundsAmbient — DROPPED (was Ambient_Wind_Desolate): §5/§6 rule the interior dead
        still, wind only at the margins as drainage the ice sheet never feels; a wind
        ambient loop on the interior contradicts its own sheet.
      baseWeatherCommonalities — Clear only. ⛔ §6: "no precipitation on the interior" (no
        snow, no blizzard, no rain, no thunderstorm) and ⛔ "no wind on the interior" (no
        Windy). "Aurora" is the sheet's narrative gloss on Clear on this hemisphere, not a
        distinct WeatherDef — none named "Aurora" exists in the live def dump. The margin
        events this table can't express (ablation drift, rime-fall, reconnection storm,
        thaw pulse) are separately owed as incident defs (sheet's Owed list).

    diseases — judgment call, recorded (the item text's "disease list per the freeze
    review" does not resolve to any file this pass could find — grepped design/Jawa for
    "freeze review", no hits). Kept Disease_Flu/Disease_Plague/Disease_OrganDecay (human
    conditions, not animal-vectored). Dropped Disease_AnimalFlu/Disease_AnimalPlague (no
    animal population to originate them — wildAnimals is empty) and the two Anomaly
    mechanite diseases (Fibrous/SensoryMechanites are shambler/Anomaly-lore diseases with
    no established connection to this sheet). Flag for the owner if a different list was
    meant.

    Still owed, explicitly NOT this item's scope (sheet's own Owed list): the 802-tile
    paint under HORRORWASTES_BIOME_DISSOLVE_1's mosaic (needs an owner-reviewed
    worldview.py render first — NOT done here); registering the def with whatever world
    tool needs an explicit biome list (C# bridge tools resolve BiomeDef by name via
    DefDatabase lookup at paint time, no hardcoded engine list —
    if a Python-side census/CSV needs this name added, that is part of the paint pass,
    not this one); tunnelers/icy insects roster and art; the equivalence-table incident
    defs (thaw pulse, calving delivery, the lost soul, rime-fall/ablation, the Dark
    drifting over); savegame re-freeze.
  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RUT_NightsideIce</defName>
    <label>the Nightside Ice</label>
    <description>Dirty white ice, geologically young and impure, on the highest ground of the deep night. It flows, it fractures, and what it swallowed it eventually gives back. There is no soil for plants to grow in. The only animals here are migrating to somewhere else -- or badly lost.</description>
    <workerClass>BiomeWorker_IceSheet</workerClass>
    <settleWarning>The nightside ice is extremely inhospitable. There is no soil for plants, almost no animal life, and no warmth anywhere but what you bring. Long-term survival is a challenge.</settleWarning>
    <!-- allowRoads TRUE by owner ruling 2026-09-07: "All of our biomes should allow roads." 91 authored road links crossed RUT_NightsideIce and were invisible - the links were structurally valid (asymmetric 0, nonAdjacent 0), the biome simply refused to draw them. -->
    <allowRoads>true</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>false</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>false</allowFarmingCamps>
    <isExtremeBiome>true</isExtremeBiome>
    <animalDensity>0</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0</plantDensity>
    <hasVirtualPlants>false</hasVirtualPlants>
    <forageability>0</forageability>
    <movementDifficulty>1.5</movementDifficulty>
    <lakeBeachTerrain>Ice</lakeBeachTerrain>
    <mudTerrain>Ice</mudTerrain>
    <texture>World/Biomes/IceSheet</texture>
    <diseaseMtbDays>90</diseaseMtbDays>
    <diseases>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_OrganDecay</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>10</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li>
        <terrain>Ice</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <Clear>100</Clear>
      <Fog>0</Fog>
      <Rain>0</Rain>
      <DryThunderstorm>0</DryThunderstorm>
      <RainyThunderstorm>0</RainyThunderstorm>
      <FoggyRain>0</FoggyRain>
      <SnowGentle>0</SnowGentle>
      <SnowHard>0</SnowHard>
      <GrayPall MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly">0</GrayPall>
      <Windy MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0</Windy>
      <Overcast MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0</Overcast>
      <Blizzard MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0</Blizzard>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <!-- WILD ANIMALS, landed 2026-09-09 by BIOME_FAUNA_ASSIGNMENT_SITTING_1.
         Source: design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/rosters/nightside_ice.json (owner
         cards 2026-09-09: "~87% eviction ACCEPTED, near-empty is correct"). Six
         shelf keeps, every one a slow (spd < 2.0, MEASURED) landform body chosen
         against §4/§6's no-eyes / no-glow / no-ordinary-silhouette bans. The comment
         above that says this list ships EMPTY described the 2026-09-07 authoring
         pass; the roster supersedes it.

         🔴 THE NODE NAME IS THE ANIMAL, THE NODE TEXT IS THE COMMONALITY.
         BiomeAnimalRecord.LoadDataFromXmlCustom reads xmlRoot.Name for the animal and
         xmlRoot.FirstChild.Value for the number, so an <li> wrapper makes FirstChild
         an ELEMENT whose .Value is null -> ArgumentNullException -> the WHOLE BiomeDef
         is discarded, silently. That shipped once and cost 26 biomes.

         ⚠️ animalDensity is 0 on this def (set by the 2026-09-07 pass, when the list
         was empty by law). At 0 these six can never spawn however high their
         commonality. The roster does not rule a density, so nothing is invented here -
         flagged to the owner as one number owed on the review sheet. -->
    <wildAnimals>
      <AA_BoulderMit MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.004</AA_BoulderMit>       <!-- boulder mit - giant, import -->
      <AA_SummitCrab MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.004</AA_SummitCrab>       <!-- summit crab - landform-giant, import -->
      <AA_RedGoo MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.003</AA_RedGoo>               <!-- red goo - small, import -->
      <AA_Terramorph MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.003</AA_Terramorph>       <!-- terramorph - medium, import -->
      <AA_Slurrypede MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.002</AA_Slurrypede>       <!-- slurrypede - medium, import -->
      <AA_TetraSlug MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.002</AA_TetraSlug>         <!-- tetra slug - giant, import -->
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <allowedPackAnimals />
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
